NAME
       rand, srand - pseudo-random numbers

SYNOPSIS
       #include <stdlib.h>

       int  rand(void);
       void srand(unsigned seed);

DESCRIPTION
       Returns a pseudo-random number between 0 and RAND_MAX. The
       sequence is the same on every run unless srand is called with a
       varying seed.

       This generator is for shuffling and sampling. Anything that has
       to be unpredictable must use crypto_random, see crypto(3).

SEE ALSO
       crypto(3), csh(1)
